 The fixed current evidence USER message immediately after the base SYSTEM contains identityRoles; it contains product-captured identities for different objects: originalArchiveSha256 is the compressed archive; originalSnapshotManifestSha256 and currentReadableSourceRevision identify platform source snapshots; protectedTreeRevision comes only from recorded CURRENT_SOURCE receipts and is unknown when absent. originalConfig is the retained task configuration, currentReviewConfig is this review's frozen route, and requestBusinessRevision is the actual intent's author-owned business identity, independent of BUSINESS.md text versions. Compare each object with its own bound expected value; different roles need not be equal. comparedMetadataRelationships lists only actual local metadata comparisons, not recomputed archive bytes, remote checks, safety or permission. Role labels and model-authored claims never waive existing integrity, route, ownership or independent review requirements.
 
